{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> The sense of <b>let YHWH please go in our midst.</b> When they journey, as in \"and I will walk among you\" (Leviticus 26:12)." "<b>For it is a stiff-necked people.</b> According to Rabbi Marinus' opinion: even though it is a stiff-necked people, and likewise \"heal my soul, for I have sinned against You\" (Psalms 41:5) — even though I have sinned against You. But in my view: heal me, for I acknowledge that I have sinned against You, and on account of my sin You made me ill; and so here: I acknowledge that it is a stiff-necked people, and You will forgive."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {1 "The name רבי מרינוס is transliterated as given; identity uncertain but the name is rendered as found in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:13.557722707Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}